comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T22:48:39.811Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed with a disposable fixture: retain an untracked file in branch so narrowing does not prune the directory, narrow the tracked leaf to visible/**, then replace branch with an outside symlink exactly at widening mkdirSync. setView(null) returns successfully and the outside sentinel becomes the tracked content. No hosted or real user data involved. Follow-up remains open; PR 96 requested materializeTree/restore changes stay scoped."
  "2026-10-12T10:56:52.209Z",pi-vcs,"Verified the current state: setView's widening and narrowing already route every working-tree mutation through the shared WorktreeMutation boundary (WorktreeMutation.write/remove/prune), which PR 96 introduced and a later change on main applied to setView; no path-based rmSync/mkdirSync/writeFileSync/chmodSync remains in setView's apply loop. Re-confirmed the original reproduction is still real against the pre-boundary implementation: with only the setView apply loop reverted to the path-based version (rmSync/mkdirSync/writeFileSync/chmodSync), swapping the retained branch ancestor for an outside-directory symlink exactly at the widening write makes setView(null) succeed and the outside sentinel becomes the tracked bytes (content replaced, mode changed to 644 via the followed chmod). The fixed engine refuses the identical swap with worktree_path_changed and the sentinel stays byte-identical."
  "2026-10-12T10:57:14.876Z",pi-vcs,"Added deterministic race tests in the shared worktree-races harness: setView narrowing (unlink), widening write (exclusive open) and widening mkdir each refuse ancestor replacement into both an outside directory and nested control state, across the pinned (between-steps and syscall boundaries) and portable (with and without O_NOFOLLOW) strategies — 24 tests, all passing. Injections reuse the same seam as the PR 96 race tests (fs syscall hooks plus the lstat observation boundary; the shared intercept helper gained an explicit observation override for the sparse-preflow shift). Each test asserts the typed worktree_path_changed refusal, byte-identical outside sentinels with unchanged modes, and that the recorded view and index are untouched by the refusal."
  "2026-10-12T10:57:15.537Z",pi-vcs,"Behavioural revert proof: with only the setView apply-loop changes reverted to the path-based rmSync/mkdirSync/writeFileSync/chmodSync implementation (and its removed pruneEmptyDirectories/chmodSync imports restored), all 24 new tests FAIL (24/24) — the widening variants report 'Missing expected exception' because the path-based widening succeeds through the swapped ancestor and overwrites the outside/control sentinel, and the narrowing variant deletes the outside sentinel through the symlinked ancestor. Restoring the boundary-routed setView makes all 24 pass. Nothing else was reverted; no dist rebuild needed since tests import engine sources directly."
  "2026-10-12T11:10:41.288Z",codex-sol,"Resuming after the previous provider quota stop. Reviewing inherited tests and documentation against the shared WorktreeMutation implementation, then independently repeating the regression matrix, setView-only behavioral revert proof, self-host equality and both release gates. The current base already routes setView writes, removals and pruning through WorktreeMutation; this branch will certify that behavior rather than duplicate the boundary."
  "2026-10-12T11:13:47.962Z",codex-sol,"Independent verification: inherited 24 sparse race cases pass. Found an additional setView publication-order defect: WorktreeMutation.prune ran after writeView/writeIndex, so a typed pruning refusal left replacement sparse metadata recorded. Moved shared-boundary pruning before view/index publication, without changing preflight or duplicating the boundary. Added widening and narrowing pruning races alongside mkdir/write/unlink races; real disposable repositories and pass-through syscall/observation hooks preserve actual filesystem operations. All 40 setView races and all 266 shared mutation tests pass, with byte-identical outside/control sentinels, unchanged modes, ObjectStoreError worktree_path_changed and unchanged recorded view/index. Behavioral revert: restore only HEAD setView => 24 pass/16 fail; restore only historical pathname setView apply loop plus necessary imports => 0 pass/40 fail. Restored the exact fixed source after both proofs. Corrected inherited documentation that had changed historical PR 96 receipt counts without new evidence; kept the original historical receipt and added current verified counts."
  "2026-10-12T11:15:03.407Z",codex-sol,"Revert-proof scope clarification after inspecting the failure output: all 40 pathname-revert cases fail, but not every between-step case reaches its observation hook once that boundary is removed. The pinned syscall widening cases directly verify overwritten outside/control bytes and the syscall narrowing cases directly verify deletion. The 16 exact HEAD-setView pruning reverts all fail the recorded-view invariant after typed refusal. Thus the original report that every variant redirected a mutation overstates the evidence; the verified receipts distinguish hook, sentinel and metadata failures. pm test --run --progress independently passed all 40 linked cases; project test-result policy is disabled, so execution was reported without persisting a test-result file."
  "2026-10-12T11:42:10.878Z",codex-sol,"The isolated-HOME npm release gate passed before the base refresh: 1461/1461 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, all-source coverage 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds, committed self-host equality, native TOON/stat-cache acceptance, production audit, identity audit, pack dry run, changelog/date and publish-attestation checks. Rebased onto the bounded single-snapshot self-host update from main; only the generated bundle conflicted, resolved by regenerating with the new writer. The historical apply-loop proof retained the current shared pruning helper: no pruning helper implementation was reverted. Implementation and focused verification are complete; releasing the claim for orchestrator review while final npm and Bun release checks run on the final commit in separate checkouts. Final gate counts and the PR link will be included in the PR and completion report. No item is closed."
